WEBVTT

00:00.248 --> 00:01.363
- [Voiceover] So we have these two graphs

00:01.363 --> 00:02.500
that look pretty similar,

00:02.500 --> 00:05.681
y equals f of x and y is equal to g of x.

00:05.681 --> 00:06.831
And what they asked us to do is

00:06.831 --> 00:10.499
write a formula for the
function g in terms of f.

00:10.499 --> 00:11.880
So let's think about how to do it

00:11.880 --> 00:13.030
and like always pause the video

00:13.030 --> 00:15.716
and see if you can work
through it on your own.

00:15.716 --> 00:17.070
All right, well, what I'd like to do is

00:17.070 --> 00:19.102
I'd like to focus on this minimum point

00:19.102 --> 00:22.700
because I think that's a
very easy thing to look at

00:22.700 --> 00:25.220
because of them have that minimum point

00:25.220 --> 00:26.241
right over there.

00:26.241 --> 00:28.203
And so we can think,
but how do we shift f?

00:28.203 --> 00:30.107
Especially this minimum point,

00:30.107 --> 00:33.984
how do we shift it to get
to overlapping with g?

00:33.984 --> 00:36.504
Well, the first thing that
might jump out of this is

00:36.504 --> 00:40.218
that we would want to shift to the left.

00:40.218 --> 00:43.144
And we'd wanna shift to the left four.

00:43.144 --> 00:46.824
So let me do this in a new color.

00:46.824 --> 00:50.051
So I would wanna shift to the left

00:50.051 --> 00:52.169
by four.

00:53.529 --> 00:55.542
We have shifted to the left by four

00:55.542 --> 00:58.342
or you could say we
shifted by negative four.

00:58.342 --> 00:59.967
Either way, you could think about it.

00:59.967 --> 01:02.465
And then we're gonna shift down.

01:02.465 --> 01:03.884
So we're gonna shift, we need to go

01:03.884 --> 01:08.138
from y equals two to y is
equal to negative five.

01:08.138 --> 01:10.263
So let me do that.

01:10.263 --> 01:13.026
So let's shift down.

01:13.026 --> 01:14.455
So we shift down by seven

01:14.455 --> 01:17.810
or you could say we have
a negative seven shift.

01:17.810 --> 01:19.215
So, how do you express g of x

01:19.215 --> 01:22.454
if it's a version of f of x
that shifted to the left by four

01:22.454 --> 01:24.009
and shifted down by seven.

01:24.009 --> 01:26.633
Or, you could say I have a
negative four horizontal shift.

01:26.633 --> 01:29.106
I have a negative seven vertical shift.

01:29.106 --> 01:33.146
Well, one thing to think
about it is g of x,

01:33.146 --> 01:37.548
g of x is going to be equal to

01:37.548 --> 01:39.644
f of,

01:39.644 --> 01:41.569
let me do it in a little darker color,

01:41.569 --> 01:46.104
it's going to be equal to f of x

01:46.104 --> 01:48.949
minus your horizontal shift,

01:48.949 --> 01:52.327
all right, horizontal shift.

01:52.327 --> 01:55.008
So x minus your horizontal shift

01:55.008 --> 01:58.637
plus your vertical shift.

01:58.637 --> 02:03.637
So plus your vertical

02:03.808 --> 02:05.689
shift.

02:05.689 --> 02:08.709
Well, what is our horizontal shift here?

02:08.709 --> 02:10.648
Well, we're shifting to the left

02:10.648 --> 02:12.192
so it's a negative shift.

02:12.192 --> 02:15.327
So our horizontal shift is negative four.

02:15.327 --> 02:16.894
Now, what's our vertical shift?

02:16.894 --> 02:18.670
Well, we went down so
our vertical shift is

02:18.670 --> 02:20.574
negative seven.

02:20.574 --> 02:22.257
So it's negative seven.

02:22.257 --> 02:23.476
So there you have it.

02:23.476 --> 02:26.227
We get g of x.

02:26.227 --> 02:28.544
Let me do that in the same color.

02:28.544 --> 02:33.544
We get g of x is equal to

02:33.834 --> 02:37.464
f of x minus negative four

02:37.464 --> 02:40.444
or x plus four

02:40.444 --> 02:43.314
and then we have plus negative seven

02:43.314 --> 02:46.146
or you can just say minus seven.

02:46.146 --> 02:47.382
And we're done.

02:47.382 --> 02:48.787
And when I look at things like this,

02:48.787 --> 02:51.966
the negative seven is somewhat,

02:51.966 --> 02:53.412
it's more intuitive to me.

02:53.412 --> 02:54.890
As I shifted it down, it made sense

02:54.890 --> 02:56.256
that I have a negative seven.

02:56.256 --> 02:57.424
But first, when you work on these,

02:57.424 --> 02:59.014
you say, "I shifted to the left.

02:59.014 --> 03:02.741
"Why is it a plus four?"

03:02.741 --> 03:04.455
And though I think about it is

03:04.455 --> 03:07.705
in order to get the same
value out of the function,

03:07.705 --> 03:09.830
instead of inputting,
so if you want to get

03:09.830 --> 03:13.150
the value of x of zero,
you now have to put

03:13.150 --> 03:15.890
x equals negative four in.

03:15.890 --> 03:17.910
And then you get that same value.

03:17.910 --> 03:20.313
You still get to zero.

03:20.313 --> 03:22.205
So that's, I know if that helps or hurts

03:22.205 --> 03:24.225
in terms of your understanding,

03:24.225 --> 03:27.151
but it often helps to try out
some different values for x

03:27.151 --> 03:30.122
and see how it actually
does shift the function.

03:30.122 --> 03:32.026
And if you just try to get
your head on this piece,

03:32.026 --> 03:34.023
the horizontal shift, I
recommended, you know,

03:34.023 --> 03:35.068
not even using this example.

03:35.068 --> 03:37.529
Use an example that only
has a horizontal shift.

03:37.529 --> 03:39.050
It will become a little more intuitive.

03:39.050 --> 03:40.605
And we do, we have many videos that go

03:40.605 --> 03:42.625
into much more depth that explain that.

03:42.625 --> 03:45.272
Let's do another example of this.

03:45.272 --> 03:48.999
So here, we have

03:48.999 --> 03:50.926
y is equal to g of x in purple

03:50.926 --> 03:52.981
and y is equal to f of x in blue.

03:52.981 --> 03:54.768
And they say given that f of x

03:54.768 --> 03:58.820
is equal to square root
of x plus four minus two,

03:58.820 --> 04:03.820
write an expression for
g of x in terms of x.

04:03.823 --> 04:05.162
So first, let's me just try to,

04:05.162 --> 04:07.774
expression for g of x in terms of f of x.

04:07.774 --> 04:08.633
We can see once again,

04:08.633 --> 04:10.978
it's just a shifted version of f of x.

04:10.978 --> 04:13.381
And remember, I'll just
write it in general.

04:13.381 --> 04:17.578
So g of x is going to be equal to

04:17.578 --> 04:22.465
f of x minus your horizontal shift

04:24.735 --> 04:29.613
plus your vertical shift.

04:29.613 --> 04:31.749
And so to go from f to g,

04:31.749 --> 04:34.414
what is your horizontal shift?

04:34.414 --> 04:36.597
Well, your horizontal shift is,

04:36.597 --> 04:38.176
if you take this point right over here,

04:38.176 --> 04:42.100
which should map to that point
once we shift everything.

04:42.100 --> 04:45.675
Your horizontal shift is two to the left

04:45.675 --> 04:48.907
or you could say it's a
negative two horizontal shift.

04:48.907 --> 04:50.961
So that should be negative two.

04:50.961 --> 04:53.116
And then, what is a vertical shift?

04:53.116 --> 04:54.962
Well, a vertical shift is removed,

04:54.962 --> 04:58.360
we go from y equals negative
two to the y equals three.

04:58.360 --> 05:01.672
So we're shifting five up.

05:01.672 --> 05:04.687
So this is a vertical
shift of positive five.

05:04.687 --> 05:06.823
So your vertical shift is five.

05:06.823 --> 05:08.095
So if we just want to write g of x

05:08.095 --> 05:11.628
in terms of f of x like we just
did in the previous example,

05:11.628 --> 05:16.047
we could say g of x is
going to be equal to f of x

05:16.047 --> 05:19.751
minus negative two which is x plus two.

05:19.751 --> 05:22.039
And then we have plus five.

05:22.039 --> 05:23.583
But that's not what they asked us to do.

05:23.583 --> 05:25.023
They asked us to write.

05:25.023 --> 05:26.207
They, whoops.

05:26.207 --> 05:28.482
They asked us to write an expression

05:28.482 --> 05:30.607
for g of x in terms of x.

05:30.607 --> 05:32.104
And so here we're actually gonna use

05:32.104 --> 05:34.786
the definition of f of x.

05:34.786 --> 05:36.342
So let me make it clear.

05:36.342 --> 05:40.147
We know that f of x is going

05:40.147 --> 05:42.377
to be equal to square root

05:42.377 --> 05:46.833
of x plus four minus two.

05:46.833 --> 05:49.635
So given that,

05:49.635 --> 05:52.513
what is f of x plus two?

05:52.513 --> 05:56.619
Well, f of x plus two
is going to be equal to,

05:56.619 --> 05:58.372
everywhere we see an x,
we're gonna replace it

05:58.372 --> 05:59.672
with an x plus two.

05:59.672 --> 06:04.672
Square root of x plus two plus four

06:05.190 --> 06:06.565
minus two

06:06.565 --> 06:09.350
which is equal to the square root of

06:09.350 --> 06:13.043
x plus six minus two.

06:13.043 --> 06:14.228
Well, that's fair enough.

06:14.228 --> 06:15.691
That's just f of x plus two.

06:15.691 --> 06:19.310
Now, what is f of x plus two plus five?

06:19.310 --> 06:24.310
So f of x plus two plus five

06:24.652 --> 06:28.368
is going to be in this thing
right over here plus five.

06:28.368 --> 06:31.131
So it's going to be
equal to square root of

06:31.131 --> 06:33.903
x plus six minus two

06:33.903 --> 06:37.029
and I'm going to add five,
with a different color.

06:37.029 --> 06:38.523
So plus five,

06:38.523 --> 06:40.543
so plus five.

06:40.543 --> 06:43.249
And so what we end up with

06:43.249 --> 06:46.255
is going to be square root of

06:46.255 --> 06:49.157
x plus six minus two plus five

06:49.157 --> 06:50.840
is going to be plus three.

06:50.840 --> 06:53.302
So that is equal to g of x.

06:53.302 --> 06:54.997
Just as a reminder, what do we do here?

06:54.997 --> 06:58.482
First, I expressed g of
x in terms of f of x.

06:58.482 --> 07:00.293
Let's say, hey, to get
from f of x to g of x,

07:00.293 --> 07:01.853
I shift two to the left.

07:01.853 --> 07:03.068
Two to the left.

07:03.068 --> 07:05.056
So we're kinda intuitive, plus two

07:05.056 --> 07:07.305
makes it a shift of two to the left.

07:07.305 --> 07:10.103
This was minus two would be
shifted two to the right.

07:10.103 --> 07:12.285
But like I just said in
the previous example,

07:12.285 --> 07:13.748
it's good to try it some x's

07:13.748 --> 07:15.559
and to see why that makes sense.

07:15.559 --> 07:17.219
And then we shifted five up.

07:17.219 --> 07:19.367
So this was g of x in terms of f of x.

07:19.367 --> 07:22.547
Then they told us what f of
x actually is in terms of x.

07:22.547 --> 07:25.543
So we said, "Okay, well,
what is f of x plus two?"

07:25.543 --> 07:28.248
F of x plus two, we
substituted x plus two for x

07:28.248 --> 07:29.571
and we got this.

07:29.571 --> 07:32.961
But g of x is f of x plus two plus five.

07:32.961 --> 07:35.445
So we took what we figured
out f of x plus two is

07:35.445 --> 07:38.081
and then we added five
and that's what g of x is.

07:38.081 --> 07:39.955
And then we are all done.
